-- examples/checks/agg-sub-ts-1-data.rofl — agg_sub_ts, a world both engines
-- answer: plain facts both load, and beside them a fixture each engine
-- refuses for a reason naming the subsumptive relation: the TypeScript
-- engine and the Rust
-- engine refuses one under well-founded semantics. The fixture does not
-- reach the world, so the two states are one.
edb(sts_e).
sts_e(a, 1).
sts_seen(A) :- sts_e(A, _).
